## 5. Clinical Interface Design — Behaviour Nudging

Drawing on Decision Architecture principles (Chee, 2026):

| Nudge Principle | Application |
|---|---|
| **Default actions** | Pre-populate recommended action per risk tier — counsellor can override |
| **Framing** | Present risk as trajectory ("risk increasing over 3 days") not just score |
| **Limited choices** | 2–3 action options per tier — reduces decision fatigue |
| **Social proof** | Show aggregate counsellor response rates to encourage timely action |
| **Observable language** | "Posting at 3am three nights this week" — not "temporal_late_night = 0.87" |

