## 6. Data Standards for Interoperability

For integration with institutional health record systems (Chee, 2026 — HL7 Chair, Singapore):

| Standard | Role in Pipeline |
|---|---|
| **HL7 FHIR** | Risk scores exported as FHIR Observation resources |
| **SNOMED CT** | Mental health condition coding |
| **ICD-10** | F32/F33 depression risk codes for clinical records |
| **LOINC** | Laboratory and clinical observation codes |

HL7 FHIR is the recommended integration standard — adopted by 90% of health information system vendors worldwide (Chee, 2026).

---

## 7. Validation Framework

| Metric | Target | Rationale |
|---|---|---|
| Sensitivity (recall) | >85% | Missing true positives is high-stakes |
| Specificity | >75% | Minimise counsellor false alarm workload |
| F1 Score | >80% | Balanced performance |
| AUC-ROC | >0.90 | Strong risk discrimination |

